opy it in there don't worry about  if the layout is going to look ugly and  if there's a lack of commerce the CTR  crate is going to make that work  automatically and at this point you've  got pretty much everything you want to  actually import this CTR and have it  work in the game we've got the right  coins that we want to put on it we've  got the right track type and we've got  all of the different track sections that  this CTR has so now you kind of want to  save it you just want to save it and you  want to have it saved as CTR bar nuttin  and then the name of whichever CTR this  is going to be so I'm going to call this  CTR test and I'm going to save it just  like that and now I'm going to open the  program and let me actually get to the  program right here so you open the CTR  creator and there's not much you really  have to do over here you just click read  CTR bar Norton dot txt that will open  the file we have just made then we say  write CTR barton no txt create write  over LS and install right over LS in ICT  3 and now when we open our CD 3 we  should be able to get the CTR to work ok  so now we're in the game and  hopefully it is all going to work right  let's see there right what's called test  yeah there we go  no it is and as you can see it works now  it is on the EP world in track which is  a CT as you can see and we do have some  different cars in it and it all works  which is really cool  now there are some errors that you might  get like there's one thing that says  track unresolved  Ct TR file I think that's how it goes  now one of the issues that may happen  with that is that some of the things  went wrong in the band mountain files  with the names of things that you had to  get in there one very common mistake  that causes that error is that the name  of the track type isn't right you get  that track unresolved TTR error when the  track type for example doesn't match the  track sections that you have posted over  here or for example if you didn